DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iinnssqquuee() and rreemmqquuee() functions encapsulate the ever-repeating task
     of doing insertion and removal operations on doubly linked lists.  The
     functions expect their arguments to point to a structure whose first and
     second members are pointers to the next and previous element, respec‐
     tively.  The iinnssqquuee() function also allows the _p_r_e_d argument to be a NULL
     pointer for the initialization of a new list's head element.

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The iinnssqquuee() and rreemmqquuee() functions conform to IEEE Std 1003.1-2001
     (“POSIX.1”).

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The iinnssqquuee() and rreemmqquuee() functions appeared in 4.2BSD.  In FreeBSD 5.0,
     they reappeared conforming to IEEE Std 1003.1-2001 (“POSIX.1”).

